{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:53:17.028Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"<permissions instructions>\nFilesystem sandboxing defines which files can be read or written. `sandbox_mode` is `read-only`: The sandbox only permits reading files. Network access is restricted.\nApproval policy is currently never. Do not provide the `sandbox_permissions` for any reason, commands will be rejected.\n</permissions instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<apps_instructions>\n## Apps (Connectors)\nApps (Connectors) can be explicitly triggered in user messages in the format `[$app-name](app://{connector_id})`. Apps can also be implicitly triggered as long as the context suggests usage of available apps.\nAn app is equivalent to a set of MCP tools within the `codex_apps` MCP.\nAn installed app's MCP tools are either provided to you already, or can be lazy-loaded through the `tool_search` tool. If `tool_search` is available, the apps that are searchable by `tools_search` will be listed by it.\nDo not additionally call list_mcp_resources or list_mcp_resource_templates for apps.\n</apps_instructions>"},{"type":"input_text","text":"<skills_instructions>\n## Skills\nA skill is a set of local instructions to follow that is stored in a `SKILL.md` file. Below is the list of skills that can be used. Each entry includes a name, description, and file path so you can open the source for full instructions when using a specific skill.\n### Available skills\n- imagegen: Generate or edit raster images when the task benefits from AI-created bitmap visuals such as photos, illustrations, textures, sprites, mockups, or transparent-background cutouts. Use when Codex should create a brand-new image, transform an existing image, or derive visual variants from references, and the output should be a bitmap asset rather than repo-native code or vector. Do not use when the task is better handled by editing existing SVG/vector/code-native assets, extending an established icon or logo system, or building the visual directly in HTML/CSS/canvas. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/imagegen/SKILL.md)\n- openai-docs: Use when the user asks how to build with OpenAI products or APIs and needs up-to-date official documentation with citations, help choosing the latest model for a use case, or model upgrade and prompt-upgrade guidance; prioritize OpenAI docs MCP tools, use bundled references only as helper context, and restrict any fallback browsing to official OpenAI domains. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/openai-docs/SKILL.md)\n- plugin-creator: Create and scaffold plugin directories for Codex with a required `.codex-plugin/plugin.json`, optional plugin folders/files, and baseline placeholders you can edit before publishing or testing. Use when Codex needs to create a new local plugin, add optional plugin structure, or generate or update repo-root `.agents/plugins/marketplace.json` entries for plugin ordering and availability metadata. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/plugin-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-creator: Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Codex's capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/skill-creator/SKILL.md)\n- skill-installer: Install Codex skills into $CODEX_HOME/skills from a curated list or a GitHub repo path. Use when a user asks to list installable skills, install a curated skill, or install a skill from another repo (including private repos). (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/.system/skill-installer/SKILL.md)\n- brainstormer: Partner with the user to turn rough ideas into well-structured concepts, then help evaluate and refine them. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/brainstormer/SKILL.md)\n- code-reviewer: Review code changes with an emphasis on correctness, clarity, maintainability, and test coverage. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/code-reviewer/SKILL.md)\n- committer: Prepare clear, scoped commit messages and help organize changes into coherent commits. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/committer/SKILL.md)\n- context-fetcher: Gather the minimum relevant context needed to begin work without overwhelming the user with unnecessary detail. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/context-fetcher/SKILL.md)\n- deep-research: Conduct deeper multi-step research, synthesis, and comparison when the user needs more than a quick answer. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/deep-research/SKILL.md)\n- deployment-reporter: Summarize deployment outcomes, risks, rollback considerations, and next checks in a way that is easy for teams to act on. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/deployment-reporter/SKILL.md)\n- docs-maintainer: Improve or create documentation so it is accurate, structured, and easy for the intended audience to use. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/docs-maintainer/SKILL.md)\n- entire:explain: Explains the intent behind source code by finding original session transcripts. Use /explain with a function, file, or line of code to understand why it exists. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/personal-local/entire/0.1.0/skills/explain/SKILL.md)\n- entire:search: Use when the user wants to find prior work, checkpoints, or agent conversations by topic, repo, branch, author, or recent time window (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/personal-local/entire/0.1.0/skills/search/SKILL.md)\n- entire:session-handoff: Use when the user wants to continue work from one agent in another agent, inspect recent sessions, or summarize a saved session or checkpoint for handoff (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/personal-local/entire/0.1.0/skills/session-handoff/SKILL.md)\n- find-skills: Helps users discover and install agent skills when they ask questions like \"how do I do X\", \"find a skill for X\", \"is there a skill that can...\", or express interest in extending capabilities. This skill should be used when the user is looking for functionality that might exist as an installable skill. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.agents/skills/find-skills/SKILL.md)\n- git-fixer: Help diagnose and recover from messy or confusing Git states without making the situation worse. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/git-fixer/SKILL.md)\n- github:gh-address-comments: Address actionable GitHub pull request review feedback. Use when the user wants to inspect unresolved review threads, requested changes, or inline review comments on a PR, then implement selected fixes. Use the GitHub app for PR metadata and flat comment reads, and use the bundled GraphQL script via `gh` whenever thread-level state, resolution status, or inline review context matters. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/eed16198/skills/gh-address-comments/SKILL.md)\n- github:gh-fix-ci: Use when a user asks to debug or fix failing GitHub PR checks that run in GitHub Actions. Use the GitHub app from this plugin for PR metadata and patch context, and use `gh` for Actions check and log inspection before implementing any approved fix. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/eed16198/skills/gh-fix-ci/SKILL.md)\n- github:github: Triage and orient GitHub repository, pull request, and issue work through the connected GitHub app. Use when the user asks for general GitHub help, wants PR or issue summaries, or needs repository context before choosing a more specific GitHub workflow. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/eed16198/skills/github/SKILL.md)\n- github:yeet: Publish local changes to GitHub by confirming scope, committing intentionally, pushing the branch, and opening a draft PR through the GitHub app from this plugin, with `gh` used only as a fallback where connector coverage is insufficient. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-curated/github/eed16198/skills/yeet/SKILL.md)\n- pr-prep: Prepare code changes for pull request submission with a focus on clarity, scope, and reviewer usability. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/pr-prep/SKILL.md)\n- product-developer: Build product features with a pragmatic balance of user needs, technical constraints, and iteration speed. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/product-developer/SKILL.md)\n- project-shipper: Drive work toward completion by clarifying scope, sequencing execution, and focusing on what is necessary to ship. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/project-shipper/SKILL.md)\n- rapid-prototyper: Help build fast, rough implementations to validate ideas quickly before investing in polish. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/rapid-prototyper/SKILL.md)\n- retro-writer: Turn project or incident history into a clear retrospective with lessons, decisions, and concrete follow-ups. (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/retro-writer/SKILL.md)\n- review-and-simplify-changes: Review a git diff or explicit file scope for reuse, code quality, efficiency, clarity, and standards issues, then optionally apply safe Codex-driven fixes. Use when the user asks to \"simplify code\", \"review changed code\", \"check for code reuse\", \"review code quality\", \"review efficiency\", \"simplify changes\", \"clean up code\", \"refactor changes\", or \"run simplify\". (file: /Users/peytonmontei/.codex/skills/review-and-simplify-changes/SKILL.md)\n- review-swarm: Parallel read-only multi-agent review of a current git diff or explicit file scope to find behavioral regressions, security or privacy risks, performance or reliability issues, and contract or test coverage gaps. Use when the user asks for a review swarm, parallel review, diff review, regression review, security review, or wants high-signal issues plus a prioritized fix path without editing files. (file: /Users/pey