-validation.md:100:In Copilot CLI, run a small prompt that changes one file, then commit it.\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:124:### 3. Run Turn 2 in the Same Copilot Session and Commit\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:126:In the same Copilot session, run another prompt that changes a different file.\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:148:### 4. End the Copilot Session\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:150:Exit the Copilot session cleanly so `session.shutdown` is written to `events.jsonl`.\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:183:- The active or most recent Copilot session shows a token total that matches `SESSION_TOTAL`, allowing only display rounding differences\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:219:- `entire status` reflects the final Copilot `session.shutdown` aggregate\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:232:- Copilot checkpoint totals are intentionally different from Claude checkpoint totals.\ndocs/architecture/copilot-token-validation.md:234:- Copilot only exposes authoritative `input/cache/output` usage as a session-wide aggregate at `session.shutdown`, so checkpoint-scoped Copilot counts are necessarily more limited.\ndocs/security-and-privacy.md:9:When you use Entire with an AI agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI), session transcripts, user prompts, and checkpoint metadata are committed to a dedicated branch in your git repository (`entire/checkpoints/v1`). This branch is separate from your working branches, your code commits stay clean, but it lives in the same repository.\ndocs/architecture/logging.md:110:- File counts (modified_files, new_files, deleted_files)\ndocs/architecture/logging.md:182:  \"modified_files\": 2,\ndocs/architecture/logging.md:202:  \"modified_files\": 5,\n"}}
