{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:58:13.065Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"task_complete","turn_id":"019e415e-af0b-75a0-b7f2-986de218ba18","last_agent_message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Managed-hook detection matches any command starting with entire\",\"category\":\"data-loss\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":23,\"endLine\":27,\"symbol\":\"entireHookPrefixes\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":315,\"endLine\":339,\"symbol\":\"isEntireHook/removeEntireHooks\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\",\"startLine\":196,\"endLine\":207,\"symbol\":\"CopilotCLIAgent.UninstallHooks\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\",\"startLine\":558,\"endLine\":625,\"symbol\":\"TestUninstallHooks_PreservesUserHooksInManagedTypes\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"The ownership predicate treats any bash command with prefix \\\"entire \\\" as an Entire-managed hook. UninstallHooks and force reinstall then remove those entries from every managed hook type, so a user-owned Copilot hook such as \\\"entire status\\\" or \\\"entire review ...\\\" would be deleted even though it is not one of this integration's hook commands. The same broad predicate also makes AreHooksInstalled report true for unrelated user hooks that happen to invoke the Entire CLI.\",\"reproduction\":\"Create .github/hooks/entire.json with an agentStop user entry whose bash is \\\"entire status\\\", then call CopilotCLIAgent.UninstallHooks; removeEntireHooks drops that user entry because it matches the \\\"entire \\\" prefix.\",\"recommendation\":\"Narrow Copilot's managed prefixes to commands this integration owns, for example \\\"entire hooks copilot-cli \\\" and the local-dev \\\"go run ... main.go hooks copilot-cli \\\" form, and keep production-wrapper support through IsManagedHookCommand.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The preservation test only uses \\\"echo user hook\\\", which does not exercise a user-owned command that starts with \\\"entire \\\".\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add uninstall and force-reinstall tests with a user hook like {\\\"bash\\\":\\\"entire status\\\"}; assert it remains while \\\"entire hooks copilot-cli agent-stop\\\" is removed/replaced.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Update cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go managed-prefix matching and add focused hooks tests.\"},{\"title\":\"Subagent stop events omit the fields required to identify the task\",\"category\":\"api-contract\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go\",\"startLine\":27,\"endLine\":39,\"symbol\":\"CopilotCLIAgent.HookNames\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go\",\"startLine\":136,\"endLine\":141,\"symbol\":\"CopilotCLIAgent.buildSubagentStop\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go\",\"startLine\":105,\"endLine\":124,\"symbol\":\"Event\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go\",\"startLine\":341,\"endLine\":359,\"symbol\":\"TestParseHookEvent_SubagentStop\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"The package installs and parses a subagent-stop hook as a SubagentEnd lifecycle event, but buildSubagentStop only sets Type, SessionID, and Timestamp. The Event contract documents ToolUseID for SubagentStart/SubagentEnd, SubagentID for SubagentEnd, and ModifiedFiles for subagent output. With those fields empty, downstream task checkpointing cannot reliably associate the completion with a parent tool invocation, subagent transcript, or touched files; at best it becomes a session-level/git-status fallback, and at worst task metadata is written under an empty or ambiguous task identity.\",\"reproduction\":\"Parse a subagent-stop payload that includes sessionId and transcriptPath; ParseHookEvent returns a SubagentEnd with empty SessionRef, ToolUseID, SubagentID, and ModifiedFiles because hookEnvelope/buildSubagentStop do not carry those fields.\",\"recommendation\":\"Either parse and populate the Copilot/VS Code subagent payload fields needed by agent.Event, or do not install/emit subagent-stop as a lifecycle event until the payload can satisfy the SubagentEnd contract.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"The existing subagent-stop test asserts only Type and SessionID, so it locks in the incomplete event shape instead of validating task identity, transcript reference, or modified files.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a subagent-stop payload fixture with transcript path, subagent/tool identifier, and modified files; assert the resulting Event populates SessionRef, ToolUseID or SubagentID, and ModifiedFiles, or assert the hook returns nil if those fields are unavailable.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"Extend cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go and lifecycle.go for subagent fields, or remove subagent-stop from HookNames/install mapping until supported.\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/copilotcli.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/generate.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/types.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/compat_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/copilotcli_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/hooks_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/lifecycle_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/copilotcli/transcript_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/event.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/hook_command.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/types.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/token_usage.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/chunking.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil/json.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil/write.go\",\"cmd/